@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .

# Alignment ledger for the metacognition (second-order epistemics) slice — GMEOW
# authoring source. Compiled to mappings/gmeow-metacognition.sssom.tsv by
# `gmeow compile-mappings`. The slice's alignments are DELIBERATELY PROSE-ONLY:
# its source literatures (Nelson & Narens' metamemory model, Flavell's
# metacognition, and the Brier-score calibration tradition) have no stable IRI
# vocabulary to map to, so the mapping set carries the scholarly grounding in its
# comment and seeds NO alignment cells. This is the same intentional
# non-mapping the inquiry slice applies to its question-type vocabulary.

gmeow:mapsetMetacognition a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-metacognition.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/metacognition" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "Metacognition-slice alignments are intentionally prose-only: the slice's grounding literatures have no stable external IRI vocabulary to map to, so no alignment cells are seeded. Grounding (by reference, Principle 5): the reflexivity turn and the metamemory monitoring/control loop follow Nelson & Narens' metamemory model; the umbrella of second-order cognition follows Flavell's metacognition; gmeow:calibration / gmeow:calibrationError follow the calibration / Brier-score tradition (a proper-scoring measure of the fit between avowed confidence and accuracy), kept solver-layer (Principle 12). The reused first-order quantities — gmeow:confidence (provenance) and credence (epistemics) — and the cross-slice bridges (inquiry's gmeow:evokes, inference's gmeow:Attack, the trust slice's gmeow:trustLevel) carry their own alignments in their home slices and are not re-mapped here." .
